# Repository line-ending policy.
#
# B2.5-P13 Corrective XV, H-XV-09 / RC-XV-09.
#
# Until this file existed the repository declared no line-ending policy at all,
# so what landed in a working tree depended on each developer's Git config.
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in its *system* config, which means
# a fresh clone on a stock Windows host silently rewrote every checked-in LF
# shell script to CRLF. The documented canonical bootstrap then failed on line
# two:
#
#     scripts/ci/run_m1_onboarding_bootstrap.sh: line 1:
#     set: pipefail: invalid option name        (exit 2)
#
# because `set -euo pipefail\r` passes `pipefail\r` to `set -o`. That was
# reproduced deterministically under bash 5.2, and it is a broken supported
# build path, not a user error: nothing the operator did caused it and nothing
# in the repository warned them.
#
# `text=auto` normalizes to LF in the object database; the explicit `eol=lf`
# rules below force LF into the working tree regardless of `core.autocrlf`, for
# every artifact whose interpreter or format requires it.

* text=auto

# Executable shell and its fixtures: CRLF here is a hard runtime failure.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
*.zsh           text eol=lf

# Container and process entry points read line-by-line by a shell or init.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
Procfile        text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
*.mk            text eol=lf
.env.*example   text eol=lf

# Formats whose consumers or hashes are newline-sensitive.
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.cfg           text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts keep CRLF: PowerShell and cmd are the consumers.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf
*.psm1          text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Binary artifacts must never be newline-translated.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
*.gz            binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.exe           binary
*.dll           binary
*.so            binary
*.dylib         binary
*.nc            binary
